        "1344039316520054784"
      ],
      "id": "1344039316520054784",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 29,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 141,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 6,
        "retweet_count": 17
      },
      "text": "Idealists often think that the best ideas win—that Darwinian idea selection selects for the highest quality ideas.\n\nInstead, it actually selects for the most viral and memetic (highest k-factor). So that means if your aim is to have the best ideas, you should often be contrarian.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1344039316520054784"
    },
