            "id": "1343025431088406529",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "@alexandr_wang @ouraring Apple watch sold like 30m units and maybe $15b in sales this year? It seems to be doing just fine for its core use case, whatever that is."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-26T01:06:28.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1342637873296633856"
        ],
        "id": "1342637873296633856",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 11,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 123,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 3,
          "retweet_count": 3
        },
        "text": "In true holiday spirit:\n\nLooking back on the past 4 years of building @scale_AI, it’s been filled with moments of great accomplishment and stretches hard work in uncertain times.\n\nI am deeply thankful for our charmed path—it’s hard to describe it as anything less than pure magic."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "752712449321644032",
        "created_at": "2020-12-17T18:16:10.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1339635515318960129"
        ],
        "id": "1339635515318960129",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 2,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 28,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 5
        },
        "text": "At Scale AI, we use machine learning to empower our data labeling pipeline. In our last blog of 2020, our ML team discusses tricks they discovered to improve @PyTorch transformer implementation with just a few lines of code. Read more: https://t.co/xvamBdE6er"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "13294",
        "created_at": "2020-06-25T15:02:28.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1276168892566495239"
        ],
        "id": "1276168892566495239",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 46,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 523,
          "quote_count": 15,
          "reply_count": 20,
          "retweet_count": 52
        },
        "text": "the number one criteria for hiring: the person really wants to work at your company"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:47:48.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335355216770736128"
        ],
        "id": "1335355216770736128",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 2,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 10,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1335355215554379776",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "7/ This gives clues as to how to solve it in big teams though:\n\n1. Maximize shared context -&gt; verticalize teams as much as possible\n2. Maximize prior -&gt; build a super strong culture"
      },
      {
        "attachments": {
          "media_keys": [
            "3_1335355019617431552"
          ]
        },
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:47:47.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335355215554379776"
        ],
        "id": "1335355215554379776",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 1,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 7,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1335355211905265664",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "6/ While the compressions are never amazing, the decompression step is where a lot goes wrong as well.\n\nIn addition to the compression, there's often limited shared context, and limited prior between Person A and Person B. https://t.co/5G4gFtSYFc"
      },
      {
        "attachments": {
          "media_keys": [
            "3_1335354925111365633"
          ]
        },
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:47:46.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335355211905265664"
        ],
        "id": "1335355211905265664",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 1,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 7,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1335355208059084800",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "5/ The version of this that nearly every coder has felt:\n\nSomeone asks you to do something, it's not *that* easy to build, and it also doesn't *really* solve the customer's problem. Double whammy of inefficiency. https://t.co/XeduGlXVXz"
      },
      {
        "attachments": {
          "media_keys": [
            "3_1335354835441340416"
          ]
        },
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:47:45.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335355208059084800"
        ],
        "id": "1335355208059084800",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 1,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 5,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1335355203655139329",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "4/ Put another way, nobody is telling the full truth. Mostly by omission, and mostly unintentionally.\n\nThis is *especially* true of customers, who, like the rest of us, are not very good information compressors. https://t.co/brl5L4FCj9"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:47:44.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335355203655139329"
        ],
        "id": "1335355203655139329",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 0,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 6,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1335354433413103616",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "3/ This process is never successful.\n\nWhenever a hand-off occurs between two people, you invariably lose about 90% of the interesting information. This hurts efficiency exponentially. Each hand-off kills nearly all the useful information."
      },
      {
        "attachments": {
          "media_keys": [
            "3_1335354415813861376"
          ]
        },
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:44:41.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335354433413103616"
        ],
        "id": "1335354433413103616",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 3,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 11,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 1
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1335352706488123393",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "2/ The *real* reason that big organizations operate less efficiently is because of bad information compression.\n\nIdeas, which are often very complex, have to pass through the very narrow window of human language, and often all the nuance is lost. https://t.co/79cPIJd2Q7"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-05T22:37:49.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1335352706488123393"
        ],
        "id": "1335352706488123393",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 61,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 183,
          "quote_count": 10,
          "reply_count": 4,
          "retweet_count": 22
        },
        "text": "I'm publishing another @scale_AI memo which meaningfully affected how many of us at Scale operated.\n\nInformation Compression\n\nBreaking it down in the thread below 👇\n\nhttps://t.co/zF3Y4Mz80Y"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-02T16:24:56.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1334171704436744192"
        ],
        "id": "1334171704436744192",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 10,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 75,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 4
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1334171703669211136",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Closing on simple advice, but so important:\n\nFocus! There are strong non-linear benefits to extreme focus. Every great business was initially focused on something so narrow it didn't seem consequential.\n\nFight the temptation to be everything to everyone. It just doesn't work."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-02T16:24:56.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1334171703669211136"
        ],
        "id": "1334171703669211136",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 6,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 47,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 5
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1334171702696181760",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "If you are a builder, adopt a mindset of short-term pessimism but long-term optimism.\n\nYou need to see the problems clear-eyed today, but it is oftentimes totally unexpected what is possible in the long-term if you remain focused.\n\nI've found that optimism often shapes reality."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-02T16:24:56.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1334171702696181760"
        ],
        "id": "1334171702696181760",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 8,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 62,
          "quote_count": 2,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 4
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1334171701844746240",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "For most of the time building @scale_AI, tactics have been more important than strategy.\n\nThe tech community has a tendency to overweigh strategy because it is more narrative and easier to think about.\n\nBut, I've found that success often comes down to extreme tactical orientation"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-02T16:24:56.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1334171701844746240"
        ],
        "id": "1334171701844746240",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 1,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 37,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 2
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1334171701001678848",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "As you scale, you will be confronted by one fork over and over: do I try to please everyone, or do I do what I think is right?\n\nIt is SO much more important to be authentic than it is to please everyone.\n\nIt is OK to be idiosyncratic sometimes.\n\nAuthenticity &gt;&gt;&gt; anything else."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-02T16:24:55.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1334171701001678848"
        ],
        "id": "1334171701001678848",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 5,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 52,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 4
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1334171700120862721",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "While this is common advice, it is the most important.\n\nSurround yourself with the BEST people. Not only people who are smart and ambitious—those who reinforce your best qualities and call you out on your worst.\n\nThis is true for teammates, customers, investors, and friends."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2020-12-02T16:24:55.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1334171700120862721"
        ],
        "id": "1334171700120862721",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 39,
          "impression_count": 0,
          "like_count": 155,
          "quote_count": 7,
          "reply_count": 3,
          "retweet_count": 6
        },
        "text": "We announced some big @scale_AI news. The illusion with this sort of news is that it always looks like an overnight success.\n\nI wanted to mention a few things I've learned along the way. I hope they'll be useful to other folks who are looking to build the future.\n\n👇Thread"
      }
